[TITLE]
AquaOptima dPHM-PINN Sprint 16 — small reference EPANET .inp fixture
in US-customary units with a HEAD-curve pump. Three-node topology:

    R1 (suction reservoir, fixed head 20 ft)
      |
      +-- PU1 (pump, HEAD curve PUMPCURVE1) --> J1
                                                |
                                                +-- P1 (pipe) --> J2 (200 GPM consumer)

Pump curve declared in ft of head vs GPM. The Sprint 16 fallback
parser converts the (Q [GPM], H [ft]) curve points to (m^3/s, m)
through the EpanetUnitSystem manifest before fitting the quadratic
``H(Q) = a0 + a1*Q + a2*Q^2`` at the static nominal speed ``s = 1``.
Hazen-Williams head loss. Solvable by aquaoptima.dphm.newton_solve
with jacobian_mode="analytic".

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elev   Demand   Pattern
 J1   0.0      0.0    ;     ; pump discharge node (no consumer)
 J2   0.0    200.0    ;     ; 200 GPM consumer

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID   Head   Pattern
 R1   20.0   ;          ; 20 ft fixed-head suction reservoir

[PIPES]
;ID   Node1   Node2   Length   Diameter   Roughness   MinorLoss   Status
 P1   J1      J2      660.0    6.0        130.0       0.0         OPEN

[PUMPS]
;ID    Node1   Node2   Parameters
 PU1   R1      J1      HEAD   PUMPCURVE1

[CURVES]
;ID          X-Value   Y-Value
 PUMPCURVE1     0.0    150.0
 PUMPCURVE1   100.0    148.5
 PUMPCURVE1   200.0    144.0
 PUMPCURVE1   300.0    136.5
 PUMPCURVE1   400.0    126.0
 PUMPCURVE1   500.0    112.5

[OPTIONS]
 Units                GPM
 Headloss             H-W

[END]
